# openOODA/INDEX — The Polyrepo

File: openOODA/docs/INDEX.oot

This file is the overview of the openOODA project as a whole. It is the
front-door copy for human visitors; the agent-facing front door is at
`openOODA/ANCHOR.oot`.

## 1. What it is

The openOODA polyrepo. Eight repositories (six public, two extracted
from `ooda/` once gemini's compiler work ships) that together form a
sovereign, capability-secure systems language for the AI era. One
`.oo` source compiles to four native targets. Every effect requires an
explicit capability token. The standard library has zero ambient
authority.

The repositories cooperate through a single `ooda` binary and a content-
addressed package registry. The compiler is the substrate; the standard
library, package manager, CLI driver, language server, and MCP server
are siblings, not dependencies.

## 2. Install

Install the toolchain:

    curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install.sh | bash

You get the `ooda` binary on `PATH`. It dispatches to the compiler,
the standard library, the package manager, the language server, and
the MCP server. One command, every repo.

## 3. Surface

The eight polyrepo repos:

| Repo        | Role                                                   | Status      |
|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
| `openOODA/` | Governance: rules, north star, RFCs, polyrepo topology | v1.0.x      |
| `ooda/`     | Compiler (`oodac`) + Gen 1 C runtime substrate         | v2.11.x     |
| `std/`      | Standard library: 8 functional domains, 173 modules     | v1.0.0      |
| `opm/`      | Package manager: CAS-by-sha, capability-tagged         | v0.8.0      |
| `cli/`      | The `ooda` binary driver, 13 subcommands                | v0.2.0      |
| `lsp/`      | Language server: 16 methods, 5 editor integrations     | v0.6.0      |
| `mcp/`      | MCP server: 23 tools, 5 tiers                          | v0.6.0      |
| `oodac/`    | Compiler (extracted from `ooda/`)                      | coming soon |
| `runtime/`  | C runtime (extracted from `ooda/`)                     | coming soon |

## 4. Where to go next

- **Submenu.** The sidebar lists each repo. Click any of them to read
  its own source-attributed page.
- **The 6 visual dropdowns on this page.** One per active repo: what
  makes each one unique at a glance.
- **The 14 capability tokens.** They appear across the LSP, MCP, and
  std/visualisations. There is no ambient authority anywhere in the
  stack.
- **The polyrepo topology.** See `openOODA/RULES.oot` §1.23 for the
  why behind the split.
